// `view()` on an `InlineArray` has the same cause as a string's `bytes()`: the view it returns is a stdlib type.
// The message used to name the array by its C typedef (`InlineArray_int32_3`) and the wrong view type (`View<T>`
// for the read-only `view()`, which returns a `ConstView<T>`).
fn int32 main() {
    InlineArray<int32>#(3) a = [1, 2, 3];
    return cast<int32>(a.view().length());
}
